<title>FRANCE: French Credit Mutuel bank 96 profit rises 21.6 pct.</title>
<headline>French Credit Mutuel bank 96 profit rises 21.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net						2.1  vs	     1.7</p>
<p>    Net banking income			  19.8  vs	    18.9</p>
<p>    General costs				 13.0  vs	    12.6</p>
<p>    Gross operating result		     6.8  vs	     6.3</p>
<p>    Payments in provisions		     1.3  vs	     1.3</p>
<p>    Shareholder equity (net)		  45.7  vs	    41.8</p>
<p>    Shareholder equity (core)		 42.3  vs	    38.4</p>
<p>    Solvency ratio (percent)		    16  vs	    16.3</p>
<p>     Of which tier one			  14.8  vs	    14.9</p>
<p>NOTE - French mutual Credit Mutuel said in a statement that the result confirmed its position as France's fifth biggest bank and that the 21.6 percent rise in net profit to 2.1 billion francs came after a payment of 876 million to the fund for general banking risks.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
